  "description": "UW ROM (SMPL 1..48) and internal E12 (E1..E21) sample slicer with slices at detected transients. The selected sample is analysed in the background (well under a second while the track is quiet); THRS sets how strong a transient must be (energy rise x1.25 at 0 to x4 at 127), SLIC the most slices, up to 32 (the strongest transients), SLNO the slice; until the analysis has the sample, SLIC equal slices. DEC 0 plays the slice once, 1..126 decay while PLAY FWD/REV/BI loops it, 127 loops forever. TIME slows the playhead with SMP-ST's splice stretch at unchanged pitch; above half way it also shortens the grains (1494 down to 909 samples). PTCH +-32 semitones."
